   = note: a dash between two clauses leaves their relationship for the reader to work out, and marks a sentence carrying more than one idea
   = help: one idea per sentence: split any sentence a reader would have to read twice. A comma, colon or semicolon in the dash's place leaves both ideas in the one sentence, so the reader is still left to untangle them
   = note: `#[warn(perfectionist::em_dash_prose)]` on by default
